  "notes": "Knuckle-walker: the torso is pitched forward by rest rotation on `body` and the head, arms and hands are rotated back to hang from it, so clips stay relative to that pose. The arms are front legs: diagonal gait with the opposite leg, elbows (`*_arm_lower`) flex in the swing like the knees. Attack rears up and slams both arms down. Lengthen the arms for a gorilla, shorten them and stand the torso more upright for a monkey, thicken the head and add a back for a silverback."
